From c0db21232f19198d257019748d61200cdabcba8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sanjay Dwivedi <sanjaykd@codeaurora.org>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2020 21:42:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] net: cdc_ether: Ensure that default MTU is minimum 2048
 
The default MTU size for a usbnet netdev is 1514. When the VLAN
packets of 1468 < size <= 1472 are sent from connected device,
they come without fragmentation as a single chunk of size greater
than 1514, resulting in the transactions failing with EOVERFLOW
error. Fix this by ensuring the minimum default MTU size for CDC
ethernet devices is 2k

Signed-off-by: Sanjay Dwivedi <sanjaykd@codeaurora.org>
---

diff --git a/drivers/net/usb/cdc_ether.c b/drivers/net/usb/cdc_ether.c
index e11f70911acc..8b09ca525c88 100644
--- a/drivers/net/usb/cdc_ether.c
+++ b/drivers/net/usb/cdc_ether.c
@@ -325,6 +325,9 @@ int usbnet_generic_cdc_bind(struct usbnet *dev, struct usb_interface *intf)
 	/* override ethtool_ops */
 	dev->net->ethtool_ops = &cdc_ether_ethtool_ops;
 
+	if(dev->hard_mtu < 2048)
+		dev->hard_mtu = 2048;
+
 	return 0;
 
